{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And a man found him, and behold, he was wandering in the field.</b> He says that he was wandering from the road and did not know where to go, and he entered the field because in the place of the pasture he was searching for them. And Scripture elaborates on this to tell us that many causes befell him that should have warranted his turning back, but he bore everything for the sake of his father, and to further inform us that the decree is true and the reasoning false, for the Holy One, blessed be He, prepared for him a guide unknown to him, to deliver him into their hands. And to this our Rabbis intended (Genesis Rabbah 84:14) when they said that these men were angels — that this entire account was not for naught, to inform us that the counsel of YHWH shall stand."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:16.946194156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}